  "goal": "Harman Neutral target adapted to the TimeEar TEA-99 open flathead. +4.5 dB @55 Hz low shelf restores the sub-bass the open fit leaks, while -1.5 dB @170 Hz trims the reported mid-bass bloom so the low end gains depth rather than thickness. +1.0 dB @400 Hz fills the slightly recessed lower mids. -1.5 dB @2.6 kHz pulls the already-forward V-shape upper mids back toward the Harman ear-gain slope instead of adding to it. -2.0 dB @6.2 kHz softens the metallic glare that varies with foam/pad. +1.5 dB @10 kHz high shelf restores the air Korean reviewers find lacking. No measurement exists for this earbud, so this is a preference baseline, not an exact correction; re-tune if you change foams.",
